WEBVTT

00:15:58.779 --> 00:16:01.339
I never shut the drawers.
I don't turn off the lights.

00:16:01.363 --> 00:16:02.869
I leave tissues everywhere ..."

00:16:02.893 --> 00:16:05.789
And you realize all the ways
you are unpleasant to live with.

00:16:05.813 --> 00:16:09.958
CA: So, let's talk about some other themes
of this sort of quest for meaning,

00:16:09.982 --> 00:16:15.352
because I think a lot of it in the book
is about reaching out into the community,

00:16:15.376 --> 00:16:16.526
building relationships

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:20.985
and the sort of transition
of trying to find something

00:16:21.009 --> 00:16:22.457
that's bigger than you are.

00:16:22.481 --> 00:16:24.402
What does that mean?

00:16:24.426 --> 00:16:28.176
DB: Well, the one that's most engaged me,
I think because of our social crisis,

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:30.001
is the lack of community.